WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:05.190
Casts can get disrupted for a variety of reasons,
sometimes schedules change, sometimes personal

00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:07.120
problems can lead an actor to drop out.

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:12.360
In some cases, things still turn out well,
or even better, for the films in question...

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:15.620
but in others, it damages the cast's chemistry
and dooms the film.

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:20.060
One of the most famous re-castings of all
time was that of Eric Stoltz in Back to the

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:20.580
Future.

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:25.840
Stoltz was the original Marty McFly, a time-traveling
teenager who's accidentally sent back to the

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:27.040
year 1955.

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:31.080
He was replaced with Michael J. Fox a little
over a month into shooting.

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:36.520
Lea Thompson, who played Marty's mom Lorraine,
told The Hollywood Reporter in 2015 that the

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:40.420
switch was "very difficult" for her, as she
was "very good friends" with Stoltz.

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:45.039
Fellow castmate Christopher Lloyd, who starred
as inventor Doc Brown, gave a radio interview

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:49.040
in 2012 and described the moment the cast
found out Stoltz was history.

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:53.040
It was during an intense period of night shooting
after he'd been working with Stoltz every

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:54.220
night for three weeks.

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:58.690
He noted that Stoltz was a "very good actor,"
but producers needed "someone with more of

00:00:58.690 --> 00:00:59.920
a comic flair" in the role.

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:04.380
Lloyd was "terrified" when he re-shot his
scenes with Fox, but he was happy that it

00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:05.400
all worked out in the end.

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:07.220
Great Scott, did it ever.

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:12.640
This young adult romance between high school
student Bella Swan and vampire Edward Cullen

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:15.240
captivated readers and moviegoers around the
globe.

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:19.660
In the first two Twilight films, the vampire
Victoria was played by Rachelle Lefevre.

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:24.800
But in the third entry, Eclipse, Victoria
didn't seem like her old self, as Lefevre

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:26.940
had been replaced by Bryce Dallas Howard.

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:32.020
Summit Entertainment and Lefevre had an awkwardly
public battle over the move, with the actress

00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:36.420
saying she was "stunned" and the studio countering
that they were "disappointed" by her "attempt

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:38.620
to make her career choices the fault of the
studio."

00:01:39.530 --> 00:01:44.000
Whether the fault lay with Lefevre's scheduling
or Summit's ruthlessness, the switch was hard

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:44.840
on her castmates.

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:49.600
Jackson Rathbone, who played Cullen coven
member Jasper Hale, noted that Lefevre was

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:51.820
a dear friend whom he was going to miss terribly.

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:56.540
And Peter Facinelli, who starred as Edward's
adoptive father, declared that he loved her

00:01:56.540 --> 00:01:57.320
"like a sister."

00:01:57.760 --> 00:02:02.100
Ang Lee picked up a Best Director Oscar for
Life of Pi, his adaption of Yann Martel's

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:06.230
novel in which a man retells the story of
his weeks surviving a shipwreck at the age

00:02:06.230 --> 00:02:06.900
of 16.

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:11.930
Adrift on the Pacific Ocean, with only a Bengal
tiger in his lifeboat for company, his story

00:02:11.930 --> 00:02:14.940
is told to a writer who is played in the film
by Rafe Spall.

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:18.040
But originally that part was filled by Tobey
Maguire.

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:22.640
Lee ended up removing Maguire after shooting
wrapped because he felt his presence took

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:23.720
away from the story.

00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:28.380
He insisted that he "loved Tobey," whom he
had worked with previously in 1997's The Ice

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:28.880
Storm.

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:32.840
But he worried that it would be distracting
to have a big movie star sitting there for

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:33.840
such a small part.

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:38.620
Irrfan Khan, who played the adult Pi, was
jarred by the recasting, as it meant he had

00:02:38.620 --> 00:02:40.000
to reshoot those scenes.

00:02:40.280 --> 00:02:44.280
He was worried about having to make a big
emotional investment all over again, but it

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:48.540
ended up working out, as he learned from his
director to use the opportunity constructively.

00:02:49.340 --> 00:02:53.740
There was a lot of pressure to deliver satisfying
sequels to The Matrix, the groundbreaking

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:56.440
1999 sci-fi cyberpunk classic.

00:02:56.800 --> 00:03:00.640
That pressure only increased when numerous
production issues led observers to wonder

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:06.510
if the series was cursed.This included numerous
deaths of cast members including Gloria Foster,

00:03:06.510 --> 00:03:10.720
who played the Oracle and who passed away
just after the filming of The Matrix Reloaded.

00:03:11.130 --> 00:03:15.800
And there was also the tragic case of Aaliyah,
who was initially cast as Zee in Reloaded.

00:03:15.819 --> 00:03:21.100
The singer and actress was killed in a plane
crash at the age of 22 in the midst of production.

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:23.020
Co-star Harold Perrineau remembered her fondly.

00:03:23.020 --> 00:03:24.550
"It was a really hard loss.

00:03:24.550 --> 00:03:29.110
Personally, it was a really hard loss, for
the community of music and entertainment,

00:03:29.110 --> 00:03:31.709
and we'll miss her."

00:03:31.709 --> 00:03:34.280
The re-audition process for Zee took many
months.

00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:38.380
Eventually Nona Gaye, daughter of singer Marvin
Gaye, was cast as her replacement.

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:43.580
The drama on the set of 1996's The Island
of Dr. Moreau is legendary.

00:03:43.960 --> 00:03:47.290
It may have started when Bruce Willis had
to drop out of the lead role and director

00:03:47.290 --> 00:03:52.060
Richard Stanley was reportedly told the only
way to save the film was to hire Val Kilmer,

00:03:52.380 --> 00:03:56.460
who ultimately realized his leverage and allegedly
started making demands.

00:03:56.720 --> 00:04:01.980
Stanley was eventually replaced by John Frankenheimer,
but that didn't stop Kilmer from causing disruptions.

00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:06.380
According to crew members, he would arrive
late, change dialogue, and bully the cast

00:04:06.380 --> 00:04:07.020
and crew.

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:11.340
One witness reported that he even intentionally
burned a cameraman "right on his face" with

00:04:11.340 --> 00:04:11.960
a cigarette.

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:15.960
Kilmer's behavior also led him to a feud with
co-star Marlon Brando.

00:04:16.240 --> 00:04:20.960
Kilmer repeatedly refused to emerge from his
trailer until Brando was on set, and Brando

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:24.240
would only come on to the set after a private
discussion with Frankenheimer.

00:04:24.569 --> 00:04:29.020
According to the director, this led to days
going by without any footage being shot, as

00:04:29.020 --> 00:04:31.880
extras sat around in their makeup and full
costumes in the heat.

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:36.440
When Charlie Hunnam and Dakota Johnson were
announced as the stars of Fifty Shades of

00:04:36.440 --> 00:04:40.380
Grey, it looked like they had the chemistry
necessary for the bondage-laced tale.

00:04:40.540 --> 00:04:43.720
Yet that chemistry wasn't enough to keep Hunnam
on board.

00:04:43.720 --> 00:04:48.320
Four weeks before shooting was set to commence,
he dropped out, citing scheduling conflicts.

00:04:48.420 --> 00:04:52.440
Johnson later explained during an interview
with David Letterman that it was "a confusing

00:04:52.440 --> 00:04:53.080
moment" for her.

00:04:53.360 --> 00:04:58.800
Hunnam's replacement, Jamie Dornan, seemed
to mollify some fan objection but by all accounts

00:04:58.800 --> 00:05:00.780
lacked the "chemistry" Johnson had with Hunnam.

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:03.139
For one thing, their press tour was low energy.

00:05:03.139 --> 00:05:05.110
"Is there than instant chemistry?

00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:07.680
No, you hate each other.

00:05:08.860 --> 00:05:09.940
He's hard to work with."

00:05:12.220 --> 00:05:16.460
And while the film was a hit, the pair didn't
generate enough sparks to win over most critics.

